# Env / secrets — real values go in .env (gitignored); .env.example stays tracked
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# ...except the arena's own verification artifacts, which MUST be tracked.
#
# `*.log` above silently swallowed both of these (found 2026-10-01, after
# VERIFICATION_FAILURE.log turned out never to have been committed in ANY of
# the four team repos across two events). The verify container writes the
# report into the workspace, then `git add -A` skips it as ignored — so the
# file existed on the runner and vanished before the push. The turn prompt and
# AGENTS.md rule 3 both tell the agent to read it next turn; it was never
# there. That is the mechanical cause of every "reported honestly, acted on by
# nobody" case in docs/INCIDENT_2026-09-23_HARNESS.md: a 7-day-old TS2307
# (alpha, 10 red CI runs) and three consecutive turns failing the same two
# test files (beta) were both cases of the agent never being told what broke.
!VERIFICATION_FAILURE.log
!VERIFICATION_NOTE.log

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
